      <description>The defining moment of the Flood of 1997 was a husband and wife being interviewed by a KCRA-TV reporter. They were standing in the back yard of their home in Weston Ranch. The cameraman minutes earlier filmed their neighborhood street where driveways were filled with Ryder, U-Haul and other rental trucks.</description>
